# Inertia.js

- Use `@inertiajs/vue3`: `Link`, `router.visit`, `useForm`, `Head` as appropriate.
- Share global props in `HandleInertiaRequests` middleware; avoid prop drilling for auth, flash, and app config.
- Controllers return `Inertia::render('Pages/...', [...])` with only the props the page needs.
- Validate input with Form Requests before passing data to Inertia responses.
- Prefer named routes with `route()` on the backend; use Ziggy or equivalent on the frontend when available.
- Use lazy/deferred props for heavy data when supported.
- Do not mix a separate SPA `axios` API layer into Inertia pages unless the project is explicitly hybrid (document in `project.mdc`).

## Boundaries

- Do not require Inertia in API-only Laravel repos without `inertiajs/inertia-laravel` installed.
- Page navigation should use Inertia visits, not full page reloads, unless linking external URLs.
